      "id": "r2",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "39. Old age stands threatening like a tigress; like enemies",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "diseases smite the body; life runs away like water from a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "broken jar; and yet, oh wonder, man acts in a way detrimental",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "to his interest ( does not try to secure moksha ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "40. The enjoyments are multifarious and of a transient",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "nature; and by them is constituted this worldly life; what for",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "should you then wander, oh people? Refrain from your actions",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "(pursuit). If our word is to be believed, concentrate your",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "mind, pure on account of the snapping of the bonds of desires,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "within its cell which can be within reach when passion is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "rooted out.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "41. That indescribable pleasure alone is the highest and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "ever abiding (lit keeping its flovour ever fresh) being in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "enjoyment of which one considers as straw ( of little impor-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "tance ) the hosts of gods such as Brahmà, Indra and others",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "and on tasting which high states (prosperity ) such as the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "sovereignty of the three worlds &c. lose all charm. O good",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "man, fix not, therefore, your affection on any other enjoyment",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "which is evanascent.[*]",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "42. That delightful city, that great king, and the circle",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of feudatory kings, and that assembly of eminent scholars at",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "his side, the ladies ( of the court ) with their faces like the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "disc of the moon, and that group of haughty princes, those",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "bards, and those stories—a bow to Death through whose",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "( destructive ) power all these things have become things of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "the past ( lit. things to be remembered ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "43. In a certain house ( also square of the dice board )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "where there were many, there ( now ) stands only one; even",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "there where there was one many followed, and there is not",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "footnote",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "* त्रैलोक्याः—v. l. Having attained that knowledge of Brahman,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "compared with which the very sovereignty of the three worlds be-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "comes unpalatable, do not fix your attachment on pleasures consist-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "ing of food, clothes and honour ( position )",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
